                                               "what":  "",
                                               "how":  "",
                                               "why":  "",
                                               "when":  "",
                                               "underTheHood":  "Workers have their own execution environment and communicate with other contexts through messages. Dedicated workers cannot directly manipulate the document DOM.",
                                               "interviewAnswer":  "Web Workers allow JavaScript to execute in background threads separate from the main browser thread. They are useful for computationally expensive work that would otherwise affect UI responsiveness.",
